WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.064
With hand-rolled i18n,

2
00:00:03.064 --> 00:00:06.325
you keep a dictionary per
language and a small t helper.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.100
It suits one or two languages,

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.865
but growth brings plurals,

5
00:00:10.865 --> 00:00:12.768
fallbacks, and file syncing.

6
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.751
General Translation
handles rendering,

7
00:00:15.751 --> 00:00:18.188
and generates and
updates translations.

8
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.204
Write the copy inside a T component,

9
00:00:22.204 --> 00:00:24.131
with counts in a Plural component.

10
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.165
Then npx gt translate writes
every language before each build.

11
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:30.892
To keep your dictionary,

12
00:00:30.892 --> 00:00:33.933
move it to JSON files
for the CLI to translate.

13
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.296
Your team now ships
Arabic with each release.
